[center][size=6][b]Death Timer - Immersive Bleedout[/b][/size]
[size=3][i]Your followers can die. You just get a chance to save them first.[/i][/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]Overview[/b][/size]
In vanilla Skyrim your followers are nearly unkillable: they drop to one knee, wait a few seconds and get back up as if nothing happened. [b]Death Timer[/b] changes that. When a follower goes down they are [b]unconscious and dying[/b], and a real-time clock starts. Heal them before it runs out and they get back on their feet and thank you. Let it run out and they are gone for good.

It doesn't stop at followers. With the included SKSE plugin, [b]named NPCs[/b] who would have died outright to an enemy fall dying instead, and can be saved the same way. Optionally, so can guards, soldiers and other unnamed friendly NPCs.

The rest of Skyrim stays safe. Essential characters and protected NPCs who aren't your followers are only [b]knocked out[/b] and recover on their own, so quests and story characters are never put at risk.

Built on [b]Andrealletius' Bleedout Revamp (ABR)[/b], reworked and expanded.

[line]

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Two paths: dying or knocked out[/b][/size]
When a friendly NPC falls, they collapse, unconscious and paralysed, and go down one of two paths:

[list]
[*][b]Dying:[/b] "[i]Lydia has fallen unconscious and is dying.[/i]" A real-time [b]Death Timer[/b] starts. Heal them before it runs out, or they die. This path covers:
[list]
[*]your [b]followers[/b] (can be switched off in the MCM)
[*][b]named NPCs[/b] saved from death by the SKSE plugin
[*][b]unnamed NPCs[/b] such as guards and soldiers, if you turn on "Rescue Generic NPCs"
[/list]
[*][b]Knocked out:[/b] "[i]Ulfric is knocked out.[/i]" Essential NPCs and protected NPCs who aren't your followers stay down, then get back up on their own after a few in-game hours. [b]They never die[/b], so quests can't break.
[/list]

Hostile NPCs, and anyone killed by a script or quest, die exactly as in vanilla.

[size=4][b]The Death Timer[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Real-time countdown, [b]60 seconds[/b] by default, adjustable from [b]10 to 300 seconds[/b].
[*]No loopholes: walking away, changing cells or waiting won't save them. Only healing will.
[*]While they're down, [b]enemies leave them alone[/b]. The fight moves on to you.
[*]Healed in time? The timer stops and they get up.
[*]Too late? They die for real. Nobody is blamed: no bounty, no murder on your record.
[*]Works with vanilla followers and [b]Simple Follower Framework[/b]. A follower who dies is cleanly released from their follower slot, so you can recruit someone new.
[*]Essential followers (e.g. [b]Serana[/b]) take the knocked-out path and can never die.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Saving named NPCs (SKSE plugin)[/b][/size]
In vanilla, a named NPC who isn't essential or protected, like Skulvar Sable-Hilt or a named traveller, simply dies when a bandit or dragon lands the killing blow. With Death Timer, that blow is caught at the last moment: [b]they fall dying instead[/b], and you have until the timer runs out to reach them.
[list]
[*]Only NPCs who are friendly to you. Enemies die normally.
[*][b]Your[/b] killing blows are never caught: if you strike them down, they die.
[*]Scripted and quest deaths are never touched.
[*][b]Rescue Generic NPCs[/b] (off by default) extends this to unnamed NPCs: guards, soldiers, travellers. Big battles can then leave several NPCs dying at once, so it's opt-in.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Rescue them[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Give Potion:[/b] activate a downed NPC to give them a healing potion from your inventory. The prompt reads [b]Give Potion +[/b] with their name below; the [b]+[/b] means a second action is available.
[*]It picks your [b]cheapest[/b] healing potion, so your good ones stay in your pack.
[*]Skips food and poisons, and skips [b]blood potions[/b] unless your patient is a vampire.
[*]Healing spells work too: Healing Hands, Heal Other, anything that restores health.
[/list]

[size=4][b]They thank you[/b][/size]
Once a rescued NPC is back on their feet, they thank you in their own voice, using Skyrim's own "thank you" lines across [b]39 vanilla voice types[/b] with no new audio: "[i]Thank you.[/i]", "[i]Many thanks![/i]", "[i]Azura bless you.[/i]", "[i]Ysmir's blessing on you.[/i]", "[i]Thanks. I guess.[/i]" and more.

[size=4][b]Search or finish them[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Search:[/b] hold the [b]Modifier Key Framework[/b] key (Left Shift, or Left Shoulder on a gamepad) and the prompt switches to [b]Search[/b]; activate to open their inventory.
[*]A harmful hit from you finishes a downed NPC. Healing never does. Finishing a follower isn't a crime; finishing anyone else is your kill, as in vanilla.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Fixes and quality of life[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Built-in stuck-bleedout fix:[/b] activating an NPC stuck in a bleedout animation helps them up.
[*][b]Off-screen recovery fix:[/b] an NPC who recovers while you're away gets up properly when you return.
[*]Fixed an original ABR bug where recovering from negative health didn't restore health correctly.
[*]Fast potion search that only looks at the potions you carry.
[*]All status notifications can be turned off.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]MCM Settings[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Recover Hours[/b]: in-game hours before a knocked-out NPC recovers on their own (default 6, 0 = never).
[*][b]Follower Death Timer[/b]: followers go down dying (default on). Off: followers are only knocked out and recover on their own.
[*][b]Time Until Death[/b]: seconds a dying NPC has before they die unless healed (default 60, 10 to 300).
[*][b]Rescue Generic NPCs[/b]: unnamed friendly NPCs can be saved too (default off).
[*][b]Use Notifications[/b]: knocked out, dying, died and potion messages (default on).
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Skyrim [b]Anniversary Edition[/b] 1.6.x or 1.7.x (the SKSE plugin is AE only)
[*]SKSE64
[*]Address Library for SKSE Plugins ([b]v13 or newer[/b] if you're on 1.7.104)
[*]SkyUI
[*]MCM Helper
[*]powerofthree's Papyrus Extender
[*]Spell Perk Item Distributor (SPID)
[*][url=https://github.com/eXgamble/Modifier-Key-Framework]Modifier Key Framework[/url] (by eXgamble): the Give Potion / Search prompt and the modifier key
[*]Andrealletius' Papyrus Functions
[/list]

[b]Optional:[/b] FormList Manipulator, for the included CACO blood potion and Vokrii compatibility.

[line]

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Do not use with Andrealletius' Bleedout Revamp (ABR).[/b] This mod replaces it.
[*][b]Not needed with:[/b] Press E to Heal Followers, NPC Stuck in Bleedout Fix. Their features are built in.
[*]Not compatible with other bleedout or follower-death overhauls that change the same behaviour.
[*]Followers managed by their own follower framework (other than vanilla or Simple Follower Framework) may be protected by that framework and survive the timer.
[*]Your currently ridden horse is never knocked out by this mod.
[*]If you're coming from ABR, remove it and make a clean save first.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]An enemy's [b]kill move[/b] may kill an NPC outright without giving them the chance to fall dying.
[*]Voice types without a vanilla "thanks" line (e.g. Serana, some custom followers) get up silently.
[/list]

[line]

